# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env, it's gitignored already.
# Every variable is optional: the warehouse, fly brain and tests run with none
# of them set. Each block says which part of the project reads it.

# --- Live Spotify tools (MCP server, DJ agent --commit) ---------------------
# From your app at https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard.
# The Selector auth flow is Authorization Code with PKCE, which is designed
# for public clients and doesn't require a client secret at all, so it's
# listed here only because the Spotify dashboard hands you both values when
# you register an app, and .env is the obvious place to keep them together.
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET is not read by any code in this project.
# Register http://127.0.0.1:8899/callback as the redirect URI (docs/OAUTH_NOTES.md).
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Warehouse location ------------------------------------------------------
# Override the warehouse the MCP server reads from.
# Defaults to ./data/selector.duckdb if unset.
# SELECTOR_DB=

# --- Teacher labelling (selector.tagger.label, docs/TEACHER.md) ------------
# Only needed to re-run the claude-sonnet-5 teacher. Costs real money.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Set only if your key isn't scoped to a single workspace.
# ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID=

# --- Hosted MCP server (api/index.py, docs/DEPLOY_MCP.md) ------------------
# Callers log in with MCP OAuth through Spotify (docs/DEPLOY_MCP.md#auth).
# Set on Vercel by scripts/setup_mcp_oauth.py: the only Spotify account
# allowed in, and the production URL (falls back to Vercel's
# VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL). Anything missing, every request gets 503
# (fails closed). For local testing without auth, set
# SELECTOR_MCP_ALLOW_NO_AUTH=1 instead; never set that on Vercel.
# SELECTOR_OWNER_SPOTIFY_ID=
# SELECTOR_MCP_PUBLIC_URL=https://selector-mcp.vercel.app
# SELECTOR_MCP_ALLOW_NO_AUTH=1
# Extra exact redirect URIs clients may register, space-separated. claude.ai
# and loopback addresses are always allowed.
# SELECTOR_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URIS=
# The old static bearer, retired. If set, it's accepted alongside OAuth
# (only for moving clients over). Leave it unset.
# SELECTOR_MCP_TOKEN=
# Live Spotify tools on the hosted server (docs/DEPLOY_MCP.md). Set on
# Vercel, not here: scripts/setup_remote_spotify.py sets the key and
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID, and the Upstash integration sets the Redis pair.
# SELECTOR_TOKEN_KEY=
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
# Set to "off" to disable the hosted Spotify tools.
# SELECTOR_REMOTE_SPOTIFY=off

# --- Private Rewind share link (web/, docs/PRIVACY.md) -----------------------
# Set on the web project in Vercel, 32+ characters. Rotating it kills old links.
# REWIND_SHARE_TOKEN=
